From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi mt76 mt7915 disable the irq tasklet before the dma cleanup

mt7915_stop_hardware() disabled the irq tasklet only after
mt7915_dma_cleanup(), which detaches the WED.  The tasklet reads the
interrupt status through the WED while one is active, so a tasklet run
on another CPU during the detach could use the WED device while it is
being cleared.  Disable the tasklet first; the MCU is already shut down
(mt7915_mcu_exit()) and nothing after it waits for the tasklet.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7915/init.c
+++ b/mt7915/init.c
@@ -1290,8 +1290,9 @@ static void mt7915_stop_hardware(struct
 	}
 	mt7915_mcu_exit(dev);
 	mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(&dev->mt76);
-	mt7915_dma_cleanup(dev);
+	/* the tasklet reads the WED, which mt7915_dma_cleanup() detaches */
 	tasklet_disable(&dev->mt76.irq_tasklet);
+	mt7915_dma_cleanup(dev);
 
 	if (is_mt798x(&dev->mt76))
 		mt7986_wmac_disable(dev);
